+# Customer App — loyalty display (read-only) notes
+
+The customer app **never** writes loyalty data. It shows the canonical
+`loyaltyAccounts/{customerId}` document (top-level, keyed by the Firebase
+Anonymous Auth UID) that the **Staff App** and **Admin Panel** maintain.
+
+## Canonical model (identical in all three apps)
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `currentStamps` | current card balance (`stamps` is the legacy alias kept in sync) |
+| `lifetimeStamps` | total stamps ever earned — **never reset by a redemption** |
+| `rewardsEarned` / `rewardsRedeemed` | reward counters |
+| `lastStampAt` | authoritative timestamp of the previous stamp |
+| `updatedAt` | last write |
+
+Visits live on `customers/{uid}`: `totalVisits`, `lastVisitAt`,
+`lastVisitTransactionId` — written exclusively by the Staff App after a
+successful stamp, so opening or refreshing the app never counts as a visit.
+
+## 12-hour stamp window
+
+One successful normal stamp per customer, per business, every 12 hours:
+
+* enforced by Firestore Security Rules inside the commit —
+  `request.time >= lastStampAt + duration.value(12, 'h')` — and by the Staff App
+  transaction, never by this UI;
+* the customer app only *reports* it: `mapLoyaltyAccount()` computes the next
+  eligible time from `lastStampAt` and the Stamps/QR screens show
+  “Next stamp available in 8h 32m (available at 9:42 PM)”, or
+  “Show my QR to earn a stamp” when the customer is eligible.
+
+`src/shared/loyaltyCanonical.ts` is a byte-identical copy of the Staff App’s
+`src/services/loyaltyCanonical.ts` and the Admin App’s
+`src/lib/loyalty/canonical.ts`; `tests/loyalty-parity.test.mjs` fails if the
+three copies (or the three `firestore.rules` files) ever diverge.
+
+## Display safety
+
+* Every timestamp goes through `toDateSafe` / `formatFirestoreDate`
+  (Firestore Timestamp, `{seconds}`/`{_seconds}`, ISO string, REST
+  `timestampValue`, epoch ms/seconds, `Date`) and renders `—` — never
+  “Invalid Date”.
+* Counters go through `safeCount` — never `NaN`/`undefined`.
+* A loyalty document that belongs to another business/customer is shown as 0
+  and never leaks data.
+* `lifetimeStamps` is displayed from the ledger-reconciled value, so a drifted
+  document (2 valid stamp transactions, `currentStamps` 2, `lifetimeStamps` 0)
+  displays 2. The app *reports* the drift; only Staff/Admin reconcile it.
+
+## Reviews
+
+`clients/{clientId}/reviews` entries carry the real menu items the customer
+selected as `selectedItems: [{ id, name }]` (plus `itemsTried` names and
+`menuItemIds`). Items come from the live menu only — no free text, no emoji, no
+demo labels. Creating a review never touches loyalty, visits or the QR token.
+
+## Tests
+
+```bash
+npm test        # 34 tests: display mapping + shared contracts + three-app parity
+npm run lint
+npm run typecheck
+npm run build
+```
+
+The runner loads the TypeScript sources directly (`node --test` with the
+`tests/register-ts-aliases.mjs` resolver hook), so no build step is required.
